    "title": "Hamilton Mill's Amy Smith leads Gwinnett County Swim League awards - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By From Staff Reports ,\n4 hours ago Flowers Crossing's Amy Smith, in red, was voted the Gwinnett County Swim League's Coach of the Year for the 2026 summer season. By Special Photo With the Gwinnett County Swim League’s summer season wrapping up, a number of top awards were announced during the county championship meet at Georgia Tech from July 10 to 12.\nHamilton Mill’s Amy Smith was voted GCSL Coach of the Year, while the Margaret Gilbert Award for teams that exhibited great sportsmanship went to Connemara, Edgewater, Apalachee Aquatics, Berkeley Hills and Steeple Station.\nTwo swimmers earned the McCall Scholarship — Evan Loo and Ana Nicolas McCalla.",
    "summary": "By From Staff Reports , 4 hours ago Flowers Crossing's Amy Smith, in red, was voted the Gwinnett County Swim League's Coach of the Year for the 2026 summer season. By Special Photo With the Gwinnett County Swim League’s summer season wrapping up, a number of top awards were announced during the county championship meet at Georgia Tech from July 10 to 12. Hamilton Mill’s Amy Smith was voted GCSL Coach of the Year, while the Margaret Gilbert Award for teams that exhibited great sportsmanship went to Connemara, Edgewater, Apalachee Aquatics, Berkeley Hills and Steeple Station.",
